import Mathlib
import Catalog.Novelty.FibonacciEntryPointDuality

/-!
# Universal Transport for the Fibonacci rank of apparition

This file **extends** the *representation/duality* program of
`Catalog/Novelty/FibonacciEntryPointDuality.lean` and the lattice-morphism structure of
`Catalog/Novelty/FibCarmichaelStructure.lean`.  There the master duality was proven,
`p ∣ F n ↔ z(p) ∣ n`, where `z(p) = fibEntry p` is the rank of apparition (entry point):
divisibility of Fibonacci numbers is *represented* by the single arithmetic function `z`.

The catalog already records that `z` is a *lattice morphism* (gcd ↦ meet, coprime product ↦
lcm).  Here we record the remaining structural facts that turn `z` into a genuine
**universal transport**, i.e. a faithful, monotone representation of the divisibility
preorder of Fibonacci numbers:

* `fibEntry_dvd_of_dvd` — **functoriality / monotonicity**: `d ∣ m → z(d) ∣ z(m)`.
  The entry point is a monotone map from the divisibility preorder `(ℕ, ∣)` to itself.
  No hypotheses: it is a corollary of the duality applied at the index `z(m)`.
* `fib_dvd_period` — **periodicity of apparition**: `p ∣ F (n + z(p)) ↔ p ∣ F n`.
  The Fibonacci-divisibility indicator of `p` is periodic with period `z(p)`.
* `fib_dvd_mod_fibEntry` — **reduction mod the entry point**:
  `p ∣ F n ↔ p ∣ F (n % z(p))`.  Divisibility only depends on `n` modulo `z(p)`.
* `fibEntry_dvd_iff_fib_dvd_imp` — **the faithfulness / transport theorem**:
  `z(p) ∣ z(q) ↔ ∀ n, q ∣ F n → p ∣ F n`.  Divisibility of entry points is *exactly*
  implication between the two Fibonacci-divisibility predicates.  Thus `z` is a faithful
  embedding of the "Fibonacci-divisibility" preorder into `(ℕ, ∣)`: it loses no information.

Together with the catalog's lattice laws, `fibEntry_dvd_iff_fib_dvd_imp` shows that `z`
realizes an order-embedding of the family of principal "Fibonacci-divisibility ideals"
`{n | p ∣ F n}` into the principal ideals of `(ℕ, ∣)` — the precise sense in which the
duality is a *universal transport*.

## Catalog synthesis

Everything is derived from `FibEntryDuality.fib_dvd_iff_fibEntry_dvd` (the master duality of
`FibonacciEntryPointDuality`).  Where `FibCarmichaelStructure` extracted the *algebraic*
(lattice) content of the duality, this file extracts its *order-theoretic / homotopical*
content: monotonicity (a functor on the divisibility preorder), periodicity (the indicator is
a function on the cyclic quotient `ℕ / z(p)`), and faithfulness (the representation is an
embedding).  No new Fibonacci-specific input is used beyond the duality itself.

